    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d336">

                <pb facs="0401" n="317" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg317"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72113/793</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Swiss Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sulzer</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Department of German</seg>
                    <lb/>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Interests XXV–9</seg>
                </opener>
                <p>The Minister of Switzerland, representing German interests in the United States,
                    presents his compliments to the Secretary of State and, referring to the
                    Legation’s memorandum dated October 18, 1918,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d336-f1"/>
                    regarding a protest of the German Government against the treatment accorded
                    German property in the Philippines, now has the honor to transmit to His
                    Excellency a carbon copy of the <hi rendition="#italic">note verbale</hi> upon
                    which the Legation’s memorandum of October 18, 1918, was based.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-27"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">November 27, 1918</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received November 29.</hi>]</dateline>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d336-a1.xml" xpointer="d336-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
